      "reason": "Triangle and reverse-triangle inequalities yield both bounds for every vector. An actual orthonormal eigenvector of T.adjoint composed with T has unit norm and squared image norm equal to its eigenvalue, which equals the square of the declared singular value. The real transpose/adjoint and determinant-to-matrix bridges are explicit. Accretivity gives D11>0 and the vector (D11,-D10) proves D11*det(D)>0 without a determinant premise. Gram determinant equals det(D)^2; both positive singular values and positive det(D) fix the root sign. The full theorem quantifies over all real matrices, s>0 and 0<=eta<1, and concludes both singular bounds, detD>0 and the sqrt bounds. Independent exact-source compile exited 0 with core axioms only."
    },
