      "reason": "The nonzero xAct contraction g^{ab} D_ai D_bj is the Euclidean Gram tensor. Exact expansion, Lagrange, Gram determinant and path determinant identities are genuine algebra. Real quantifier elimination universally proves squared norm bounds for u=norm(v), w=norm(Ev), z=<v,Ev>, a strict homotopy gap, and the final positive fourth-root eigenvalue-product bound. The standard real spectral theorem transfers the vector bounds to both eigenvalues. For every path parameter t in [0,1], the strict gap excludes a nonzero kernel; determinant polynomial continuity plus the intermediate-value theorem fixes its sign from s^2>0. No target or invertibility is assumed. Full frozen stdout and empty stderr inspected."
